       "nl": "One entry is a perfume sold under its own name; flankers and concentrations (EDT, EDP, parfum, intense) are versions of it.",
       "sel": "Entries come from fetched references: all 112 Wikidata items that are perfumes with an English Wikipedia article (101 are named perfumes; 11 are not and are left out), every row of Wikipedia's List of perfumes, every fragrance winner table and the Fragrance Hall of Fame on Wikipedia's FiFi Award page, and the fragrance lists on the Wikipedia pages of Guerlain, Chanel, Francis Kurkdjian and the Osmothèque. A perfume sits in a family kind only where a fetched page states its family (Wikipedia articles, Perfume Intelligence house pages, or the perfume's Fragrantica or Parfumo page, with the family taken from the first word of the label and the page's launch year matching the entry); every other perfume is here. 423 perfumes are now in family kinds and 182 remain here. Every remaining perfume was searched for on Wikipedia and then on Fragrantica one at a time; for these there is no page, a page with no family or no launch year, a label outside the mapping (such as a bare \"Aromatic\"), or a page year that differs from the entry's year, often by one. Fragrantica's and Fragrances of the World's own databases could not be read whole, so the list is not their complete catalogue. Covers 182 of the 605 named perfumes in this department; complete: 112 of 112 Wikidata perfume items read, 265 of 265 rows of the List of perfumes read, 318 of 318 FiFi winner rows read; the Guerlain, Chanel and Kurkdjian lists cover the notable fragrances those pages name, and the Osmothèque list covers 13 named perfumes of over 3,000 in the collection.",
