       "nl": "One entry is a single aroma compound or a trade-named specialty chemical; grades and dilutions of one compound are versions.",
       "sel": "Wikipedia's Perfume ingredients category (155 pages, compounds only), the aroma compounds named in Wikipedia Aroma compound, and the trade names on Wikipedia's List of fragrance compounds with grade and dilution variants merged. Family sections are the compiler's chemical and olfactive grouping: Michael Edwards' Fragrance Wheel (Wikipedia, fetched; Floral, Amber, Woody, Fresh with Citrus, Water, Green, Aromatic, and Fruity) classifies finished perfumes, and no fetched page gives odour classes for raw materials, so its labels are not used here. Years are given only where a fetched page states them (Hedione, Iso E Super, Galaxolide, Calone, musk xylene, muscone, ethyl vanillin). Covers 282 entries; the category's non-compound pages (concepts such as fixative, fragrance oil, gourmand, herbal distillate, nag champa) and its natural materials are in the other kinds or left out, and the List of fragrance compounds repeats compounds in many grades, so a page count is not comparable.",
